SWEET USB 3 SuperSpeed, DEFAULT ON for the gs101 gadget (patch 0173, boot-arg sweetusb3=0 opts out to the HS-only gadget; user order R27, 2026-10-29).
With sweetusb=2 (and sweetusb3 absent or =1) the gs101 gadget starts with DCFG.DEVSPD = SuperSpeed (4) instead of high speed (0), and keeps
everything else as ABL left it (no USB 3 PHY, PMU or clock writes; NUMP kept). At ConnectDone: SuperSpeed -> ep0 max packet 512,
SuperSpeed descriptors (bcdUSB 0x0320, bMaxPacketSize0 9, BOS with USB 2.0 extension + SuperSpeed capability with U1/U2 exit
latency 0, 1024-byte bulk + endpoint companions, bMaxPower in 8 mA units), bulk DEPCFG max packet 1024 burst 0; high speed -> the
existing HS descriptors and ep0 64 byte for byte. SET_SEL is acknowledged with a "USB3 GAP:" line, SET_ISOCH_DELAY with an informational "USB3:" line (as Linux dwc3), U1/U2
SET/CLEAR_FEATURE are stalled with a "USB3 GAP:" line. If the gadget is not configured 10000 ms after RUN (no ConnectDone, or a failed SuperSpeed enumeration), or a ConnectDone
speed contradicts the programmed bulk max packet, the controller is stopped (RUN_STOP = 0, wait DEVCTRLHLT), soft-reset and
restarted at high speed once (ud_restart; "USB3 GAP: ..."), so the USB log link survives a failed SuperSpeed link. The SuperSpeed
path writes new values to DCFG.DEVSPD, DCTL.RUN_STOP (fallback) and the max-packet fields of DEPCMDPAR0 for ep0/bulk; the first
two go through an allowlist (ud_ss_wr). sweetusb3 is parsed once (starts at 1, PE_parse_boot_argn returns TRUE only when the arg is present: pexpert/gen/bootargs.c, xnu-8796.141.3): the default prints "SWEET USB3: default ON (sweetusb3=0 opts out)", an explicit sweetusb3=0 prints "SWEET USB3: sweetusb3=0: opted out, HS-only gadget (explicit)", and a requested SuperSpeed (the default or sweetusb3=N, N != 0) on a gs101 sweetusb=2 start that does not reach ud_hw_init prints "USB3 GAP: sweetusb3=N ignored: gadget not started", and an explicit sweetusb3=N on any other path does too; the default on sweetusb=0/1 or non-gs101 stays silent. The silent `!pn` return of sweet_usb_gadget_start now has its own USB3 GAP line. Read-only reports before and after the soft reset (GUSB2PHYCFG, GUSB3PIPECTL, DCFG, DSTS, GHWPARAMS0/7, GTXFIFOSIZ(1)) printed
as "SWEET USB3:" lines. Every field is cited in the code (Linux v6.12 dwc3 core.h/gadget.c/gadget.h/ep0.c, ch9.h, composite.c,
f_ecm.c, hub.c; ABL decompile offsets); spec super docs/specs/SPEC-USB3-SUPERSPEED.md, research super docs/research/102.
Hardware status [obs-hw, docs/runplans/usb3-ss.md]: observed only with an EXPLICIT sweetusb3=1: usb3-ss-1 (USB 2 link: connected at high speed, no fallback) and usb3-ss-2 (USB 3 link: connected at SuperSpeed). The default-ON path (no sweetusb3 arg, R27) and the 10 s HS fallback (ud_ss_fallback/ud_restart) are unobserved [guess: the default takes the same `usb3 == 1` branch as the explicit arg]; a hardware run is pending.
